{"id":"ALG-P07","workedExamples":[{"id":"ALG-P07-we-01","title":"Multiply two monomials: 3x^2 · 4x^3 (multiply coefficients, ADD exponents)","steps":[{"prompt":"We want 3x^2 · 4x^3. A monomial has two parts: a coefficient (the number) and a power of x. Name the two coefficients and the two exponents.","reveal":"Coefficients are 3 and 4. Exponents are 2 and 3. These two parts are handled by DIFFERENT rules — do not treat them the same way."},{"prompt":"Handle the coefficients. Do we add or multiply 3 and 4?","reveal":"Multiply: 3 · 4 = 12. The coefficients are factors multiplied together, so they multiply. (A common error is adding them to get 7 — that is wrong.)"},{"prompt":"Handle the exponents. For x^2 · x^3, do we add or multiply the exponents 2 and 3?","reveal":"Add: x^2 · x^3 = x^(2+3) = x^5. Same base means add exponents. (A common error is multiplying them to get x^6 — that is wrong.)"},{"prompt":"Combine the coefficient result and the exponent result into one monomial.","reveal":"12x^5. The 12 came from MULTIPLYING (3·4) and the 5 came from ADDING (2+3). Two parts, two different rules."},{"prompt":"State the final answer and the rule in one line.","reveal":"3x^2 · 4x^3 = 12x^5. Rule: coefficients MULTIPLY, exponents ADD. Not 7x^5 (added coefficients) and not 12x^6 (multiplied exponents)."}]},{"id":"ALG-P07-we-02","title":"Distribute a monomial over a polynomial: 2x(3x^2 + 4x − 5) (hit EVERY term)","steps":[{"prompt":"We want 2x(3x^2 + 4x − 5). How many terms are inside the parentheses, and how many products will we form?","reveal":"Three terms: 3x^2, +4x, and −5. The monomial 2x must multiply ALL THREE, so we form three products. Dropping any term is the partial-distribution error."},{"prompt":"First product: 2x · 3x^2. Multiply coefficients, add exponents.","reveal":"2 · 3 = 6 and x^1 · x^2 = x^3, so 2x · 3x^2 = 6x^3."},{"prompt":"Second product: 2x · 4x. Multiply coefficients, add exponents.","reveal":"2 · 4 = 8 and x^1 · x^1 = x^2, so 2x · 4x = 8x^2."},{"prompt":"Third product: 2x · (−5). Keep the sign; x stays to the first power.","reveal":"2 · (−5) = −10 and the x is just x^1, so 2x · (−5) = −10x. Do NOT skip this term."},{"prompt":"Write all three products in standard order and state the answer.","reveal":"2x(3x^2 + 4x − 5) = 6x^3 + 8x^2 − 10x. All three terms are present — the monomial reached every term, not just the first."}]}],"problems":{"p1":[{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A batting cage is a rectangle. Its width is 2x feet and its length is the scoring expression (3x + 5) feet. Its area is 2x(3x + 5). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^2 + 10x","5x^2 + 10x","6x^2 + 5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^2 + 10x"},"misconceptionMap":{"5x^2 + 10x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","6x^2 + 5":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to BOTH terms: 2x·3x and 2x·5.","2x·3x = 6x^2 (2·3=6, exponents 1+1=2); 2x·5 = 10x. Combine."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A hitter's projected total bases scales by 3x^2 times the expression (2x + 4): the product is 3x^2(2x + 4). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^3 + 12x^2","5x^3 + 12x^2","6x^3 + 4"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^3 + 12x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"5x^3 + 12x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","6x^3 + 4":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Multiply 3x^2 by each term inside.","3x^2·2x = 6x^3 (3·2=6, 2+1=3); 3x^2·4 = 12x^2."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"An infield patch is 4x feet wide and (2x^2 + 3x − 1) feet long. Its area is 4x(2x^2 + 3x − 1). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^3 + 12x^2 − 4x","8x^3 + 12x^2","6x^3 + 12x^2 − 4x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^3 + 12x^2 − 4x"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^3 + 12x^2":"partial-distribution","6x^3 + 12x^2 − 4x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 4x must hit all THREE terms.","4x·2x^2 = 8x^3; 4x·3x = 12x^2; 4x·(−1) = −4x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-baseball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A run-projection model multiplies 5x^2 by the scoring expression (3x^2 + 2x − 4): the product is 5x^2(3x^2 + 2x − 4). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["15x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2","15x^4 + 10x^3","8x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"15x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"15x^4 + 10x^3":"partial-distribution","8x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 5x^2 to every term; multiply coefficients, add exponents.","5x^2·3x^2 = 15x^4; 5x^2·2x = 10x^3; 5x^2·(−4) = −20x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-softball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A practice net is a rectangle 2x feet wide and (4x + 3) feet long. Its area is 2x(4x + 3). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^2 + 6x","6x^2 + 6x","8x^2 + 3"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^2 + 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^2 + 3":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·4x = 8x^2 (2·4=8, 1+1=2); 2x·3 = 6x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-softball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A hitter's projected RBIs scale by 3x times (3x + 5): the product is 3x(3x + 5). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["9x^2 + 15x","6x^2 + 15x","9x^2 + 5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"9x^2 + 15x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 15x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","9x^2 + 5":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 3x to both terms.","3x·3x = 9x^2 (3·3=9, 1+1=2); 3x·5 = 15x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-softball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A field tarp is 3x feet wide and (2x^2 + 4x − 2) feet long. Its area is 3x(2x^2 + 4x − 2). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^3 + 12x^2 − 6x","6x^3 + 12x^2","5x^3 + 12x^2 − 6x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^3 + 12x^2 − 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^3 + 12x^2":"partial-distribution","5x^3 + 12x^2 − 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 3x must reach all three terms.","3x·2x^2 = 6x^3; 3x·4x = 12x^2; 3x·(−2) = −6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-softball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"softball","prompt":"A scoring model multiplies 4x^2 by (2x^2 + 3x − 5): the product is 4x^2(2x^2 + 3x − 5). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^4 + 12x^3 − 20x^2","8x^4 + 12x^3","6x^4 + 12x^3 − 20x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^4 + 12x^3 − 20x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^4 + 12x^3":"partial-distribution","6x^4 + 12x^3 − 20x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 4x^2 to every term.","4x^2·2x^2 = 8x^4; 4x^2·3x = 12x^3; 4x^2·(−5) = −20x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-basketball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A practice court section is 2x feet wide and (5x + 4) feet long. Its area is 2x(5x + 4). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["10x^2 + 8x","7x^2 + 8x","10x^2 + 4"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"10x^2 + 8x"},"misconceptionMap":{"7x^2 + 8x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","10x^2 + 4":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·5x = 10x^2 (2·5=10, 1+1=2); 2x·4 = 8x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-basketball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A scorer's projected points scale by 4x times (2x + 3): the product is 4x(2x + 3). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^2 + 12x","6x^2 + 12x","8x^2 + 3"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^2 + 12x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 12x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^2 + 3":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 4x to both terms.","4x·2x = 8x^2 (4·2=8, 1+1=2); 4x·3 = 12x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-basketball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A floor decal is 3x feet wide and (3x^2 + 2x − 4) feet long. Its area is 3x(3x^2 + 2x − 4). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["9x^3 + 6x^2 − 12x","9x^3 + 6x^2","6x^3 + 6x^2 − 12x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"9x^3 + 6x^2 − 12x"},"misconceptionMap":{"9x^3 + 6x^2":"partial-distribution","6x^3 + 6x^2 − 12x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 3x must hit all three terms.","3x·3x^2 = 9x^3; 3x·2x = 6x^2; 3x·(−4) = −12x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-basketball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"basketball","prompt":"A scoring model multiplies 5x^2 by (2x^2 + 4x − 3): the product is 5x^2(2x^2 + 4x − 3). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["10x^4 + 20x^3 − 15x^2","10x^4 + 20x^3","7x^4 + 20x^3 − 15x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"10x^4 + 20x^3 − 15x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"10x^4 + 20x^3":"partial-distribution","7x^4 + 20x^3 − 15x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 5x^2 to every term.","5x^2·2x^2 = 10x^4; 5x^2·4x = 20x^3; 5x^2·(−3) = −15x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-soccer-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A training grid is 2x meters wide and (3x + 6) meters long. Its area is 2x(3x + 6). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^2 + 12x","5x^2 + 12x","6x^2 + 6"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^2 + 12x"},"misconceptionMap":{"5x^2 + 12x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","6x^2 + 6":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·3x = 6x^2 (2·3=6, 1+1=2); 2x·6 = 12x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-soccer-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A striker's projected goals scale by 3x times (4x + 2): the product is 3x(4x + 2). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["12x^2 + 6x","7x^2 + 6x","12x^2 + 2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"12x^2 + 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"7x^2 + 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","12x^2 + 2":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 3x to both terms.","3x·4x = 12x^2 (3·4=12, 1+1=2); 3x·2 = 6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-soccer-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A pitch banner is 4x meters wide and (x^2 + 3x − 2) meters long. Its area is 4x(x^2 + 3x − 2). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["4x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x","4x^3 + 12x^2","5x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"4x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x"},"misconceptionMap":{"4x^3 + 12x^2":"partial-distribution","5x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 4x must reach all three terms.","4x·x^2 = 4x^3; 4x·3x = 12x^2; 4x·(−2) = −8x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-soccer-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"soccer","prompt":"A model multiplies 5x^2 by (2x^2 + 2x − 6): the product is 5x^2(2x^2 + 2x − 6). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["10x^4 + 10x^3 − 30x^2","10x^4 + 10x^3","7x^4 + 10x^3 − 30x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"10x^4 + 10x^3 − 30x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"10x^4 + 10x^3":"partial-distribution","7x^4 + 10x^3 − 30x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 5x^2 to every term.","5x^2·2x^2 = 10x^4; 5x^2·2x = 10x^3; 5x^2·(−6) = −30x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-football-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A practice zone is 2x yards wide and (6x + 3) yards long. Its area is 2x(6x + 3). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["12x^2 + 6x","8x^2 + 6x","12x^2 + 3"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"12x^2 + 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^2 + 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","12x^2 + 3":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·6x = 12x^2 (2·6=12, 1+1=2); 2x·3 = 6x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-football-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A back's projected yards scale by 4x times (3x + 5): the product is 4x(3x + 5). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["12x^2 + 20x","7x^2 + 20x","12x^2 + 5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"12x^2 + 20x"},"misconceptionMap":{"7x^2 + 20x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","12x^2 + 5":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 4x to both terms.","4x·3x = 12x^2 (4·3=12, 1+1=2); 4x·5 = 20x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-football-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A field banner is 3x yards wide and (2x^2 + 5x − 1) yards long. Its area is 3x(2x^2 + 5x − 1). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^3 + 15x^2 − 3x","6x^3 + 15x^2","5x^3 + 15x^2 − 3x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^3 + 15x^2 − 3x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^3 + 15x^2":"partial-distribution","5x^3 + 15x^2 − 3x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 3x must hit all three terms.","3x·2x^2 = 6x^3; 3x·5x = 15x^2; 3x·(−1) = −3x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-football-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"football","prompt":"A yardage model multiplies 4x^2 by (3x^2 + 2x − 5): the product is 4x^2(3x^2 + 2x − 5). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["12x^4 + 8x^3 − 20x^2","12x^4 + 8x^3","7x^4 + 8x^3 − 20x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"12x^4 + 8x^3 − 20x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"12x^4 + 8x^3":"partial-distribution","7x^4 + 8x^3 − 20x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 4x^2 to every term.","4x^2·3x^2 = 12x^4; 4x^2·2x = 8x^3; 4x^2·(−5) = −20x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-volleyball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A practice court strip is 2x feet wide and (4x + 5) feet long. Its area is 2x(4x + 5). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^2 + 10x","6x^2 + 10x","8x^2 + 5"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^2 + 10x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 10x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^2 + 5":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·4x = 8x^2 (2·4=8, 1+1=2); 2x·5 = 10x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-volleyball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A hitter's projected kills scale by 3x times (5x + 2): the product is 3x(5x + 2). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["15x^2 + 6x","8x^2 + 6x","15x^2 + 2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"15x^2 + 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^2 + 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","15x^2 + 2":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 3x to both terms.","3x·5x = 15x^2 (3·5=15, 1+1=2); 3x·2 = 6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-volleyball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A net banner is 4x feet wide and (2x^2 + 2x − 3) feet long. Its area is 4x(2x^2 + 2x − 3). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^3 + 8x^2 − 12x","8x^3 + 8x^2","6x^3 + 8x^2 − 12x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^3 + 8x^2 − 12x"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^3 + 8x^2":"partial-distribution","6x^3 + 8x^2 − 12x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 4x must reach all three terms.","4x·2x^2 = 8x^3; 4x·2x = 8x^2; 4x·(−3) = −12x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-volleyball-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"volleyball","prompt":"A model multiplies 5x^2 by (3x^2 + 2x − 4): the product is 5x^2(3x^2 + 2x − 4). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["15x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2","15x^4 + 10x^3","8x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"15x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"15x^4 + 10x^3":"partial-distribution","8x^4 + 10x^3 − 20x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 5x^2 to every term.","5x^2·3x^2 = 15x^4; 5x^2·2x = 10x^3; 5x^2·(−4) = −20x^2."],"difficulty":3},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-neutral-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A garden bed is a rectangle 2x feet wide and (4x + 7) feet long. Its area is 2x(4x + 7). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^2 + 14x","6x^2 + 14x","8x^2 + 7"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^2 + 14x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 14x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^2 + 7":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms.","2x·4x = 8x^2 (2·4=8, 1+1=2); 2x·7 = 14x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-neutral-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A quantity scales by 3x times (2x + 6): the product is 3x(2x + 6). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^2 + 18x","5x^2 + 18x","6x^2 + 6"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^2 + 18x"},"misconceptionMap":{"5x^2 + 18x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","6x^2 + 6":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 3x to both terms.","3x·2x = 6x^2 (3·2=6, 1+1=2); 3x·6 = 18x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-neutral-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A poster is 4x inches wide and (2x^2 + 3x − 2) inches long. Its area is 4x(2x^2 + 3x − 2). Which expression equals that area?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x","8x^3 + 12x^2","6x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x"},"misconceptionMap":{"8x^3 + 12x^2":"partial-distribution","6x^3 + 12x^2 − 8x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 4x must hit all three terms.","4x·2x^2 = 8x^3; 4x·3x = 12x^2; 4x·(−2) = −8x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p1-neutral-04","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":1,"sport":"neutral","prompt":"A model multiplies 5x^2 by (2x^2 + 4x − 1): the product is 5x^2(2x^2 + 4x − 1). Which expression equals it?","visual":null,"choices":["10x^4 + 20x^3 − 5x^2","10x^4 + 20x^3","7x^4 + 20x^3 − 5x^2"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"10x^4 + 20x^3 − 5x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"10x^4 + 20x^3":"partial-distribution","7x^4 + 20x^3 − 5x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["Distribute 5x^2 to every term.","5x^2·2x^2 = 10x^4; 5x^2·4x = 20x^3; 5x^2·(−1) = −5x^2."],"difficulty":3}],"p2":[{"id":"ALG-P07-p2-baseball-01","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"A scoring expression is modeled as 2x(4x + 3). Expand it to standard form. Which expression is correct?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^2 + 6x","6x^2 + 6x","8x^2 + 3"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^2 + 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^2 + 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^2 + 3":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 2x to both terms; coefficients multiply, exponents add.","2x·4x = 8x^2; 2x·3 = 6x."],"difficulty":1},{"id":"ALG-P07-p2-baseball-02","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"Expand the modeled total 3x(2x^2 + 5x − 2) to standard form. Which expression is correct?","visual":null,"choices":["6x^3 + 15x^2 − 6x","6x^3 + 15x^2","5x^3 + 15x^2 − 6x"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"6x^3 + 15x^2 − 6x"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^3 + 15x^2":"partial-distribution","5x^3 + 15x^2 − 6x":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients"},"hints":["The monomial 3x hits all three terms.","3x·2x^2 = 6x^3; 3x·5x = 15x^2; 3x·(−2) = −6x."],"difficulty":2},{"id":"ALG-P07-p2-baseball-03","version":1,"skillId":"ALG-P07","phase":2,"sport":"baseball","prompt":"Expand 4x^2(2x + 3) to standard form. Which expression is correct?","visual":null,"choices":["8x^3 + 12x^2","6x^3 + 12x^2","8x^3 + 3"],"answer":{"kind":"choice","value":"8x^3 + 12x^2"},"misconceptionMap":{"6x^3 + 12x^2":"adds-exponents-and-coefficients","8x^3 + 3":"partial-distribution"},"hints":["Distribute 4x^2 to both terms.","4x^2·2x = 8x^3 (4·2=8, 2+1=3); 4x^2·3 = 12x^2."],"difficulty":2},{"id